From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:17:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: apple: Cover every Apple SoC Orchard runs on

Without this driver suspend-to-idle looks fine and keeps the tick and
CLOCK_MONOTONIC running, so any sleep over three minutes kills the service
watchdogs on wake. The states are the WFI these SoCs already idle in. Build
it for the 4K platform as well. Tested only on T8010.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
index 94a103d05a66..f782bf2f0c7f 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
@@ -48,9 +48,17 @@ static struct cpuidle_driver apple_cpuidle_driver = {
 	.state_count = 2,
 };
 
-/* The SoCs whose suspend-to-idle has been tested with this. */
+/* WFI is what these SoCs idle in anyway, so this asks nothing new of them. */
 static const char *const apple_cpuidle_socs[] __initconst = {
+	"apple,s5l8960x",
+	"apple,t7000",
+	"apple,t7001",
+	"apple,s8000",
+	"apple,s8003",
+	"apple,s8001",
 	"apple,t8010",
+	"apple,t8011",
+	"apple,t8015",
 	NULL
 };
 
